I want something similar for these stages.

Assistant: Yes, I'm familiar with GitLab CI and its pipeline stages and dependencies. In a similar way, you can define dependencies between stages in your JSON based query language by using a `dependsOn` field in the `PipelineStage` interface. Here's an updated TypeScript schema that includes the `dependsOn` field:
```css
interface SearchQuery {
  stages: PipelineStage[];
}

type PipelineStage =
  | SummarizeStage
  | SlackSearchStage
  | DocumentSearchStage
  | LimitStage
  | SortStage;

interface SummarizeStage {
  $summarize: {
    field: string;
    size: number;
  };
  dependsOn?: string[];
}

interface SlackSearchStage {
  $slackSearch: {
    channel: string;
    text: string;
  };
  dependsOn?: string[];
}

interface DocumentSearchStage {
  $documentSearch: {
    field: string;
    operator: "=" | ">" | "<" | ">=" | "<=" | "!=";
    value: string | number | boolean;
  };
  dependsOn?: string[];
}

interface LimitStage {
  $limit: number;
  dependsOn?: string[];
}

interface SortStage {
  $sort: {
    [field: string]: 1 | -1;
  };
  dependsOn?: string[];
}
```
In this updated schema, we've added an optional `dependsOn` field to each `PipelineStage` interface. The `dependsOn` field is an array of strings that specifies the names of the stages that the current stage depends on.

When you define a search query, you can specify the dependencies between stages by setting the `dependsOn` field in each stage that has dependencies. The values in the `dependsOn` array should correspond to the names of the stages that the current stage depends on.

For example, if you have a `SlackSearchStage` that depends on the results of a `DocumentSearchStage`, you can set the `dependsOn` field in the `SlackSearchStage` like this:
```bash
{
  "$slackSearch": {
    "channel": "#general",
    "text": "Results of document search",
  },
  "dependsOn": ["$documentSearch"]
}
```
This will ensure that the `SlackSearchStage` only runs after the `DocumentSearchStage` has completed.

